      "id": "wfpedia:aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZwZWRpYS5jb20v",
      "name": "The Ultimate Endo Farming Guide ^4.1 ​",
      "text": "Type: community_guide\nSource: WFPedia\nURL: https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/endo/basics\nDescription: Endo Farming Guide\nContenu: The Ultimate Endo Farming Guide | WFPedia Skip to content WFPedia Search K Main Navigation Home Guide Collection About Changelog Contact Us Privacy Policy Appearance Table of Contents Back to top Sidebar Navigation Endo Guide Introduction Basics & Mechanics Roles & Builds Khora Nidus Nekros Procedures Khora Nidus Nekros Video Resources Share this page Contents Farm Endo Warframe Endo Trade Endo Farm Aya Warframe Aya Trade Aya From credits Profit-Taker Comm. to speedruns Buy me a coffee Support the development https://ko-fi.com/meb154 The Ultimate Endo Farming Guide ^4.1 ​ DISCORD If you’ve gone through the guide, have any questions or feedback, or need players to farm with, you can to join our Warframe Endo Discord server here: https://discord.gg/endo Introduction ​ This guide will go over an endgame farm so we will be focusing on the highest efficiency possible . We will not be covering beginner-friendly endo farms such as Zariman bounties. Rathuum arena is a mission on Sedna. The objective is to kill 25 executioners to complete the mission. Players saw that enemies dropped Endo, sparking interest in Nekros, who boosts Endo drops with Desecrate. Squad Composition ​ In the current meta, we will be using Nidus, Khora, and 2 Nekros. Khora uses Ripkas / Prisma Skana (with incarnon) for DPS while making use of her 4th ability, Pilfering Strangledome , to increase the endo drops. Nidus pulls the enemies into Khora’s cages. 2 Nekros help with manipulating spawns by standing and aiming at designated spots, while keeping their 3rd ability Desecrate active to improve the endo drops. How To Play ​ Choosing the correct map ​ Current endo farming meta is done on planet Sedna in the mission Vodyanoi instead of Yam to avoid dealing with temporarily invincible enemies, also its easier for Nidus to pull. Getting More Endo ​ The biggest increase in endo is by having one party member with the Mod Drop Chance Booster . This is because the endo drops from the enemies count as mod drops. This stacks with the Steel Path booster for a 200% increase in the chance for endo drops. It is possible to get 5,000 endo in one mission if you have both. Ways to obtain a mod booster: Purchasing any Prime Access Reward from daily Sortie Reward from weekly Archon Hunt Rotation reward from weekly Circuit Purchase from Baro Ki’Teer 1999 Calendar (occasional) Rotation reward from weekly The Descendia You can LFG for all those missions in our Warframe Endo Discord Server. We will also notify you when Baro brings mod booster. TIP Only one player in the party need mod booster, booster effect does not stack with each other. Dismemberment ​ SKIP This section is for explaining why and how, you can skip this section if you are not interested in learning the mechanics and rather just do the farm. Bodies ​ An enemy can only be dismembered up to 2 times. The bodies can be: Upper & lower body Leg, arm, and head Only the upper and lower body can be desecrated with Nekros and generates more loot, the leg/arm/head cannot. Weapon ​ Weapons must have over 50% (50% will not work) of their physical damage (IPS) as slash damage to guarantee a dismemberment of an enemy. It does not guarantee the valid dismemberments (upper & lower bodies). However, you can continue to attack the corpse to dismember it even after it's dead. There is roughly a 0.7s time limit for dismembering an enemy after it’s killed. After this time window, the bodies will get desecrated by Nekros. NOTE Executioner Zura only gets dismembered upon killing with initial damage, you will not be able to dismember them by attacking the corpse after it's dead. Elements ​ You want to avoid modding Heat and Cold on your weapon. Heat can burn the body and make it difficult for Nekros to desecrate. Corrosive can melt the bodies too, but it's mostly visual only. Cold can freeze the enemy and make the corpse unable to dismember. Pager Next page Khora ☕︎ Powered by VitePress, sugarat/theme Copyright © 2024-present, WFPedia",
