      "id": "wfpedia:aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZwZWRpYS5jb20v",
      "name": "The Ultimate Aya Farming Guide ^5.0 ​",
      "text": "Type: community_guide\nSource: WFPedia\nURL: https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/aya/introduction/basics\nDescription: Farm aya\nContenu: The Ultimate Aya Farming Guide | WFPedia Skip to content WFPedia Search K Main Navigation Home Guide Collection About Changelog Contact Us Privacy Policy Appearance Table of Contents Back to top Sidebar Navigation Aya Guide Introduction Basics Procedure Rolling Stages Volt Nova Wisp & Nidus General Tips Builds Volt Nova Wisp Nidus Weapons Companion & Archwing Misc. Video Resources Credits Share this page Contents Farm Endo Warframe Endo Trade Endo Farm Aya Warframe Aya Trade Aya From credits Profit-Taker Comm. to speedruns Buy me a coffee Support the development https://ko-fi.com/meb154 The Ultimate Aya Farming Guide ^5.0 ​ ​ WARNING FOR THE TIME BEING, THIS METHOD DOES NOT WORK. DUE TO THE RECENT WARFRAME UPDATE (v40.0.0) BOUNTIES WILL CHANGE EVERY TIME IT IS REPLAYED, MEANING WE CAN'T GET THE SAME QUICK BOUNTY INFINITELY. JOIN THE DISCORD FOR MORE INFORMATION https://discord.gg/fjDrJp6nhN ​ Aya is a crucial resource in Warframe, particularly for those aiming to collect relics and prime parts. Players need large amounts of Aya to maximize their farming efficiency. This guide will walk you through the quickest and most efficient method to farm Aya. DISCORD COMMUNITY If you’ve gone through the guide, have any questions or feedback, or need players to farm with, you can join our Warframe Aya Discord Server here: https://discord.gg/fjDrJp6nhN Basics ​ Aya farming is not a new concept within Warframe, but it has developed over the years. There are many ways to farm Aya, which include: Opening relic packs (Syndicate, Open Worlds vendors, Teshin) Missions (Aya can be found anywhere you can get a relic as a mission reward) Bounties in Open Worlds (mostly high-tier ones) Rerolling bounties (which is what this guide focuses on) In this guide, we will be using the Bounty Reroll method. This involves rerolling a specific bounty (queuing up a particular bounty) until we obtain the desired stages (which you will learn about later in the guide). The idea is to achieve super easy and fast stages so that completing the entire bounty won’t take more than 2 minutes for the average player. Squad Composition ​ The squad consists of 2 main roles Lead and Support where Volt & Nova are leading the run with Wisp & Nidus as strong supports. Volt: The core and usually the squad’s host, responsible for crucial tasks like hacking consoles, initiating assassinations, escorting and speeding up the drone as well as teammates. Nova: Helps speed up crucial parts of the run (i.e. Drone/Prisoner escort) with strategic portal ( Wormhole ) placement, making the farm significantly faster. Wisp: Provides team support by placing Health and Haste motes ( Reservoir ) that boost Health, Movement speed, and Fire rate. Her motes greatly enhance teams pace and survivability. The role is expects player to help team pick up the slack wherever needed (Assisting during assassination, helping with caches, hacking consoles whenever needed etc.). Nidus: Provides team support by boosting Wisp's Ability strength via Parasitic Link significantly boosting the buffs from her motes. He also assists the team in other stages similar to Wisp picking up slack wherever needed. Correct Bounties ​ Open-World Bounties in warframe have limited mission types referred to as stages and of these stages some are time-gated (i.e. Armored vault and Liberate the Camp) some are staggered or lack ease of access (i.e. Exterminate/Sabotage/Cave Caches) and then there are some stages which are independent of these limiting factors making them really fast and easy to complete with some setup. Out of all possible stages in Cetus bounties, the stages mentioned below are the fast ones. Capture Caches (surface not cave) Rescue Drone Assassinate All bounty types have a fixed final stage by design, which determines the set of possible mission types they can include. The two bounty types (commonly referred to as Correct bounties) listed below stand out because of this: Capture the Grineer Agent Find the Hidden Artifact These bounties have one of the fast stage types as their fixed final stage, Capture for \"Capture the Grineer Agent\" and Caches(surface or cave) for \"Find the Hidden Artifact.\" Because of this, at Tier 5 these bounties have a chance of including all 5 fast stages, making them particularly efficient for farming. WARNING Do not confuse Capture the Grineer Agent with Capture Their Leader or Find the Hidden Artifact with Reclaim the Stolen Artifact .These are different bounties, and the latter in each case will not have a chance to have all 5 fast stages. Why are we only going after Tier 5 bounties? Tier 5 bounties offer the highest drop chance for Aya, which is our main focus. How to easily dentify the Good Bounty? Both the Correct bounties will have the same icon with an Ayatan sculpture in it as shown below. General Tips and Utility ​ Dialogue-skip ​ Host should always skip NPC dialogues after completing stages to save time, after each stage player can enter the Nightwave tab then leave to do so. NOTE Leaving the Nightwave tab is what triggers Nora’s dialogue, which cancels Cetus NPC dialogue this means players can to open Nightwave tab towards the end of a stage (when no further assistance is required of you), wait for the reward audio signaling stage completion, then exit instantly for the fastest dialogue skip. Gear Required ​ Focus School: Madurai (way - Sling Strength ) for Wisp and Nidus is a must have as you will learn later and Zenurik with ways like Wellspring and Inner Might are good for energy upkeep for Nova and Volt players. Operator Arcanes: Magus Anomaly paired with Magus Lockdown are useful for holding mobs. NOTE Spamming Magus Anomaly casts has an unusual interaction where it makes it difficult for the host to open menus, which can interfere with Nightwave skipping and queueing missions. To avoid this, don’t spam Anomaly continuously, leave a small gap between casts. Instead, you can follow these steps: cast Magus Lockdown, then use Magus Anomaly a few times to pull enemies in, then switch to Archwing and hold them with your 3rd ability, which slows them in place. Keep aggro up by shooting your primary around them. Magus Lockdown drops a small grenade on cast, which can rarely sometimes kill a few of the mobs. To counter this drawback, make sure that after casting Lockdown you pull the enemies away from the center of the Lockdown cast, where the grenade lands. Lockdown is optional and purely for QoL, so feel free to skip it if you run into this issue often. Protea Specter: Provides Energy Orbs for Nidus and Wisp during the mote buffing phase, while also supplying energy and ammo for the entire squad. NOTE Make sure that while crafting these specters you equip battery weapons only (i.e. Shedu, Bubonico etc.) to avoid specters consuming the ammo for themselves. Sometimes the specters can go inactive during night time due to vomes nearby if you notice your specter is inactive locate and kill vomes around the tent. Ciphers: Speed up hacking of interactables (e.g., Prisoner and Drone), saving valuable time during missions. You can consume up to 180-200 or more ciphers for a full rotation depending on your speed, make sure you build surplus amounts. NOTE Do not use alternatives like parazon mods (i.e. Auto breach ) they are slower compared to simply using ciphers. Energy/Ammo Pads: Frequent ability use by Volt and Nova makes Energy Pads essential in critical moments. Ammo Pads are especially helpful for sustaining the Akarius, given its low ammo reserves and high usage rate. Useful Settings ​ Enemy Highlights: Enable the Enemy Highlights settings option and choose a bright color (e.g Cyan, Pink) and putting the Enemy Highlight Intensity to a value of 50-100 makes it easier to see enemies. Enabling the Ally Highlights settings option allows you to see the Rescue Target and the Active Drone (not before hacking). Visual Effects Intensity: Lower Visual Effects Intensity in the Accessibility settings to make objective markers easier to see. At high intensity, markers can appear overly bright and obscure the Capture target, making it harder to spot from a distance. A slight misfire could cause you to fail the bonus objective, so keep the intensity fairly low for better visibility. Pager Next page Rolling Stages ☕︎ Powered by VitePress, sugarat/theme Copyright © 2024-present, WFPedia",
      "source": "Guide communautaire — WFPedia",
