      "id": "wfpedia:aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZwZWRpYS5jb20v",
      "name": "Secura Lecta Credits Farming Guide ^1.0.3 ​",
      "text": "Type: community_guide\nSource: WFPedia\nURL: https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/credits/secura-lecta/introduction/basics\nDescription: Credits Farming Guide (Secura Lecta)\nContenu: Secura Lecta Credits Farming Guide | WFPedia Skip to content WFPedia Search K Main Navigation Home Guide Collection About Changelog Contact Us Privacy Policy Appearance Table of Contents Back to top Sidebar Navigation Secura Lecta Credits Farming Guide Introduction Basics Mechanics Builds Chroma Xaku (Duo) Operator Weapons Companions Procedures Chroma Xaku Dealing with Acolytes Misc Graphic settings FPS Dips Ideal Credits Fissures Side Room Tier List Q&A Credits Share this page Contents Farm Endo Warframe Endo Trade Endo Farm Aya Warframe Aya Trade Aya From credits Profit-Taker Comm. to speedruns Buy me a coffee Support the development https://ko-fi.com/meb154 Secura Lecta Credits Farming Guide ^1.0.3 ​ WARNING As of update 42.0.10 this method no longer works. The specific interaction that made the Lecta drop so many credits was patched. kabir, a Warframe Endo discord member achieved this incredible pace during a double credits weekend of may 2026. Link to post DISCORD COMMUNITY If you’ve gone through the guide, have any questions or feedback, you can to join our Discord Server here: https://discord.gg/endo Introduction ​ This method involves using the Secura Lecta for its passive ability, leveraging Chroma’s Effigy to provide additional credit drops, and combining Xaku or Zenurik’s slow effects with certain death animations to generate even more credits. The best node for this strategy was determined to be Titan, Saturn. However, there are a few things to be aware of before jumping into the farming process. Since FPS directly affects enemy movement speed, how fast enemies are pulled in by Ensnare, and attack speed, higher rates generally correlate with higher FPS. See here for more information. Solo runs require practice and can be difficult to run smoothly without refining the process. Chroma typically experiences FPS dips after about 20 minutes in duo runs due to how slow applies. An exact theory for why this happens is still being developed. It’s also worth noting that everything in this guide comes from extensive hours of testing and credit farming, but not every possible interaction or piece of information has been discovered. The details shared here reflect the combined experience and opinions of the guide creators and may not represent the absolute best or only way to farm efficiently. This document is meant to serve as a foundation; a starting point for players to build upon and refine. We encourage you to experiment, adapt, and develop your own strategies to make the farm even more efficient and consistent. Pager Next page Mechanics ☕︎ Powered by VitePress, sugarat/theme Copyright © 2024-present, WFPedia",
      "source": "Guide communautaire — WFPedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/credits/secura-lecta/introduction/basics",
      "sourceType": "community_guide",
      "expertCategory": "community_guide",
      "validationStatus": "community_reference"
    },
    {
      "id": "wfpedia:aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cud2ZwZWRpYS5jb20v",
      "name": "The Ultimate Solo Index Guide ​",
      "text": "Type: community_guide\nSource: WFPedia\nURL: https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/index/basics\nDescription: Credit Farming Guide\nContenu: The Ultimate Solo Index Guide | WFPedia Skip to content WFPedia Search K Main Navigation Home Guide Collection About Changelog Contact Us Privacy Policy Appearance Table of Contents Back to top Sidebar Navigation Ultimate Index Guide Introduction Basics & Mechanics Builds Excalibur Umbra Operator Wisp (Duo) Procedure Run Procedure Share this page Contents Farm Endo Warframe Endo Trade Endo Farm Aya Warframe Aya Trade Aya From credits Profit-Taker Comm. to speedruns Buy me a coffee Support the development https://ko-fi.com/meb154 The Ultimate Solo Index Guide ​ Acquiring enough credits is a crucial step in maximizing mods in Warframe. You'll need a large amount of credits to fully upgrade your mods. To achieve this, there are two main options: Profit Taker and Index. Profit Taker missions offer higher credit gains over time but require focus and attention. On the other hand, the Index can be completed alone with less effort, making it a convenient choice. Drops from Prodman, he spawns at ~1h into the run, and there is only 1 Prodman per session. If you’ve read the guide, have any questions or comments, or want to find people to run with, here’s a link to our Warframe Endo Community: https://discord.gg/endo We’re happy to help clarify things about Index Farms that weren’t covered by this guide. The Basics ​ This section should give you a basic idea of what the Index is. The Index is a mission in Warframe where players can earn credits and prizes. It takes place in an arena on Neptune and involves fighting against elite Corpus enemies. Before starting the Index, we choose how many credits to invest. The investment amount determines how many points are required to deposit. When you successfully reach these points, you will receive your invested credits back and earn extra profits according to the listed rewards. Why Index? ​ Although Profit Taker and Secura Lecta missions offer higher credit gains over time, they require focus and attention. On the other hand, the Index can be completed alone and semi AFK, making it a convenient choice. Mechanics ​ There are two maps available for the Index: The map we will be using for this tactic is Outpost. To access this map, it’s highly suggested that you go to a DOJO or RELAY and start the mission from there, as it will force you to spawn into the right map. Important details In order to not get flagged as being AFK, you can press 5 (operator) every 1 minute or so. This will have the same effect as the typical moving 5m every ~2 minutes. However, if you are going for a long endurance run, you might want to press 5 every 10-15 seconds in case your Umbra dies. Pager Next page Excalibur Umbra ☕︎ Powered by VitePress, sugarat/theme Copyright © 2024-present, WFPedia",
      "source": "Guide communautaire — WFPedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.wfpedia.com/posts/index/basics",
